%% The path that must never double-book, and the path that must survive a
%% gateway that lies. Two diagrams in one file because they are one story.

sequenceDiagram
    autonumber
    participant A as User A
    participant B as User B (99 others)
    participant API as api
    participant PG as Postgres
    participant GW as gateway
    participant W as worker

    Note over A,B: 8:00:01 — everyone taps seat F12

    par The burst
        A->>API: POST /api/holds  F12
        API->>PG: INSERT seat_claims ON CONFLICT DO NOTHING
        PG-->>API: 1 row
        API-->>A: 201  hold_id, expires_at
    and
        B->>API: POST /api/holds  F12
        API->>PG: INSERT seat_claims ON CONFLICT DO NOTHING
        PG-->>API: 0 rows
        API-->>B: 409 SEAT_UNAVAILABLE
    end

    Note over PG: the unique index decided it.<br/>No lock, no lease, no read-then-write gap.

    A->>API: POST /api/bookings
    A->>API: POST /api/bookings/:ref/pay
    API->>PG: INSERT payments (PENDING) — BEFORE calling charge
    API->>GW: POST /charge (no await)
    API-->>A: 202 Accepted

    Note over GW: 2–15s pass. 8% of the time,<br/>this next message arrives twice.

    GW->>API: callback evt_001 SUCCEEDED
    API->>PG: INSERT callback_events ON CONFLICT (event_id) DO NOTHING
    PG-->>API: 1 row → apply
    API->>PG: seat_claims HELD → BOOKED, booking CONFIRMED
    API-->>GW: 200

    GW->>API: callback evt_001 (duplicate)
    API->>PG: INSERT callback_events ON CONFLICT DO NOTHING
    PG-->>API: 0 rows → DUPLICATE
    API-->>GW: 200
    Note over API,PG: No second payment.<br/>No second confirmation.<br/>Revenue counted once.

    Note over A,W: The other ending — nobody pays
    W->>PG: UPDATE seat_claims SET state='EXPIRED'<br/>WHERE state='HELD' AND expires_at < now()
    Note over PG: seat is green again.<br/>Readers already treated it as free —<br/>the sweeper just makes the map honest.
